<<~ ahu slot=`#/b5-browser-twins-reader-five-lares`>>

! b5-browser-twins (row T13) — Reader-Five: Lares (Tasked Spirit)

Read in full: packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts (1962 lines; bootUnderLock 490-1946, all of it) and the node counterparts in packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts (3770 lines; every twin region read), plus edge-shadow-ring.ts, nexus-standing.ts, hearth-dial-pin.ts, node-plugin-resolution.ts, worn-mount.ts, persona-act-store.ts, lease-observation.ts, mesh wiki-activation.ts, tw5 vessel-residency-wiring.ts. Line numbers as of main checkout 27bc0cb6b.
Fences kept: read-only, no suites, no boots.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/findings`>>

!! FINDINGS (top)

F1 [correctness, fails CLOSED; not a key/cross-face leak] An admitted browser leaf resolves a DIFFERENT island on every boot after the admit boot.
* Admit boot (browser 630-642): nexusPubkey = admittedJoineeIsland({hearthGatePubKey, hearthIslandKind, hearthIslandScope}); runApplyAdmitPayload seeds the KEL inception onto that island's board (706-716).
* The admit rides ONE boot only (packages/lararium-web/src/main.ts 373: takeStashedAdmit). The bootstrap it writes (729-747) keeps hearthGatePubKey/hearthGatePin but NOT hearthIslandKind/Scope.
* Every later boot: admit undefined -> nexusIdentity(nexusStandsAt) with anchorGateKey: null, no genesis (619-623, 644). Island = the vessel's own key (or walk.nexusAid). carryPersonaKelUpTheGradient only reads islands BELOW own (none), so the chain seated at the hearth's island is absent from the own-key board -> the Binding Gate throws "persona-KEL chain ... absent" (1249-1251). The leaf bricks on its second boot.
* The node closed this exact defect: nodeNexusStandsAt (nexus-standing.ts 55-84) re-reads the admit's island snapshot (hearth-dial-pin.ts HEARTH_ISLAND_KIND/SCOPE/GATE_KEY tiddlers in the bootstrap) every boot; init.ts 300-310's comment states "Seeding one island and reading another HALTS the Binding Gate fail-closed at first boot".
* UNPROVEN: no test reboots after an admit. nexus-board-climb-at-leaf.test.ts 387-410 is a source-grep ("toContain('admittedJoineeIsland({')"), and every whole-boot unit test halts at catalog-ready or bootstrap-kept. Needs a red (admit boot, then a second boot with no admit, assert same nexusPubkey) before any cure. The cure is the cut itself: persist the island snapshot in the bootstrap and read it through ONE mesh stage (see C1).

F2 [correctness, UI-state; not security] Browser wiki-switch (1539-1552) tests `if (active)` on the object ensureActive returns. WikiActivationResult is {ok:true}|{ok:false,cause,detail} (mesh wiki-activation.ts 45-47), always truthy. A FAILED activation still flips activeSurfaceId, places open-wiki, and returns `active: {ok:false,...}` (an object, not a boolean). Node reads `active.ok` (3209) and returns cause/detail. Typecheck cannot see it. The cut (C8) cures it by construction.

F3 [watch, not a fault] Catalog failure policy diverges. Node: pointer file written only after repo.flush(); a missing catalog doc is TERMINAL (resolveBootDoc). Browser: catalogUrl in boot keys is written later (loadGenesis, 1099) with NO flush; a missing doc re-founds BLANK with a loud console.error (loadFoundedCatalogOrWarn). A crash between pointer and doc flush reads in the browser as a false DATA-AMNESIA and silently orphans every registered wiki. This is a deliberate leaf tolerance, but the unflushed pointer is the same hazard node measured. NEEDS-RULING, do not collapse the body.

No key reaches a surface and no cross-face read leaks in what I read. atomSeed/wornAtomSeed are zero-filled after use (717, 780, 1213, 1369). siblingAside / deviceAside fail closed before the first fleet read (562, 1479).

<<~/ahu>>

